<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  page="privacy"
  title="Privacy Policy — InFocus"
  description="InFocus collects no data. No account, no analytics, no ads, no tracking."
>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="meta">Effective October 29, 2026 · Applies to InFocus 1.0 for iPhone</p>

  <div class="notice">
    <p><strong>In short: InFocus collects no data.</strong> There is no account, no analytics, no advertising and no tracking, and the app does not connect to the internet.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Who makes InFocus</h2>
  <p>InFocus is made and published by Franklin Guevara, an independent developer (“I”). If you have a question about this policy, write to <a href="mailto:support@infocustempo.com">support@infocustempo.com</a>.</p>

  <h2>What is collected</h2>
  <p>Nothing. I do not collect, receive, store, sell or share any personal information or usage data. The app contains no analytics, crash-reporting, advertising or other third-party software, and it makes no network requests.</p>

  <h2>What stays on your iPhone</h2>
  <p>To work, the app keeps the following only on your device:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your presets and favorites</li>
    <li>Your session history: start and end times, timer type, rounds, notes and the optional intention you type</li>
    <li>Your settings, such as sounds, voice, haptics and daily goal</li>
    <li>The timer that is currently running, so it can continue after the app is closed</li>
  </ul>
  <p>I cannot see this information. It is included in your iPhone backups, which Apple handles under its own privacy policy, and it is deleted when you delete the app.</p>

  <h2>Permissions the app asks for</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Alarms</strong>: so the end of a focus block, a break or a workout rings with your iPhone locked or in Silent mode. Alarms are scheduled on your device.</li>
    <li><strong>Notifications</strong>: only if you decline alarms, to alert you at the same moments.</li>
    <li><strong>Live Activities</strong>: to show the running timer on the Lock Screen and in the Dynamic Island.</li>
    <li><strong>Siri and Shortcuts</strong>: if you use them, Apple processes your voice request; the app only receives which timer to start.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The app does not use your location, contacts, photos, camera, microphone or health data.</p>

  <h2>Exporting your history</h2>
  <p>If you choose Settings → Export history, the app creates a CSV file and hands it to the iOS share sheet. Where it goes next is up to you.</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>Because the app collects no information from anyone, it collects none from children.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If a future version changes what the app does with data, I will update this page and its effective date before that version is released.</p>
</BaseLayout>
